Date: Thu, 9 Apr 2026 19:29:31 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add tool.execute and tool.list RPC methods to gateway

Adds direct tool execution capability to the OpenClaw gateway, enabling
callers to invoke any tool (coding or gateway) without going through the
LLM agent loop. Used for trajectory replay and validation.

New RPC methods:
- tool.execute: Execute a tool by name with arguments
- tool.list: List all available tools with schemas

Both methods merge coding tools (exec, read, write, edit, apply_patch,
process) with gateway tools (web_search, web_fetch, memory_search, etc.)
into a unified tool set. Coding tools are created with hardcoded container
defaults matching the Scale Modal sandbox layout.

Gated behind operator.admin scope for security.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
